## Gate-3 remediation
sáb 22 ago 2026 (sesión 21:55–02:05 -03) — fixes for Oracle Gate-3 findings 1-4 on d3e3f55+1e98e02

### Finding 1 [HIGH] — sandbox wired into execute_bash
- ToolRegistry now holds `bash_sandbox: Option<Sandbox>`; `new`/`with_timeout`/`with_read_limit`
  arm `Sandbox::new(SandboxConfig::new(cwd))`. Builders: `with_workspace`, `with_sandbox`, `without_sandbox`.
- execute_bash: Guard::check_chain FIRST, then `sb.apply(&mut cmd)` (ordering per sandbox.rs contract).
- SandboxError::Unsupported/Setup → ToolError::Sandbox with actionable message (fail-closed: command NOT executed).
- Spawn failure while armed → ToolError::Sandbox hinting blocked user namespaces + KITTY_SANDBOX=off opt-out.
- Loud opt-out: env KITTY_SANDBOX=off honored ONLY when set; tracing::warn EVERY activation.
- Test: tools::bash_write_outside_workspace_denied_by_sandbox_with_negative_control
  (Guard-passing `cp` outside fs_allow FAILS sandboxed + victim untouched; succeeds without sandbox).

### Finding 2 [HIGH] — Landlock TRUNCATE bypass closed
- apply_landlock no longer pins ABI::V1. Probes kernel ABI (landlock_create_ruleset VERSION probe):
  >=3 → ABI::V3 rights (adds REFER v2 + TRUNCATE v3); V1/V2 exact fallback for older kernels;
  cap at V3 so untested deny-by-default rights (ioctl_dev v5, etc.) stay off. Kernel here reports ABI 9.
- seccomp truncate/ftruncate entries stay unconditional (needed inside allow-roots); path-level policy
  now actually comes from Landlock on ABI>=3. ABI<3 kernels remain DAC-only for truncate (documented limitation).
- REFER side-effect documented at apply_landlock: cross-root renames (/tmp <-> workspace) may newly fail — fail-closed, accepted.
- Test: sandbox::truncate_outside_fs_allow_denied_with_negative_control
  (libc::truncate(2) via re-entrant child payload op "truncate"; unsandboxed control OK, sandboxed → CHILD-TRUNCATE-ERR).

### Finding 3 [MEDIUM] — RLIMIT_AS configurable
- KITTY_SANDBOX_MEM_MB is now the AUTHORITATIVE input, parsed at SandboxConfig build
  (parse_mem_limit_mb: positive integers only; invalid → tracing::warn + DEFAULT_MEM_LIMIT_MB=512).
- Doc: bench contexts should set >=4096 (rustc/javac/JVM reserve multi-GB VIRTUAL address space; RLIMIT_AS caps VA not RSS).
- Test: sandbox::pure::parse_mem_limit_mb_accepts_positive_integers_only.

### Finding 4 [LOW] — tgkill removed from seccomp allowlist
- Dropped from SECCOMP_PURE_ALLOW; module docs updated to "kill/tkill/tgkill/ptrace/pidfd_*" (docs match reality).
- Pure test extended: tgkill AND tkill asserted absent from the allowlist.

### BONUS FIX (discovered by new wiring, blocking finding 1)
- Double-fork middle process held std's exec-error channel open until the WORKLOAD finished:
  parent spawn() blocked for the entire command duration and tokio::time::timeout around
  spawn+wait NEVER fired (strace: runtime thread stuck in recvfrom(13) for 10s of `sleep 10`).
- Fix: middle closes all inherited fds >2 before waitpid (containment::close_inherited_fds);
  grandchild unaffected (independent fd tables, CLOEXEC copies close at execve).
- Regression test: tools::bash_timeout_still_fires_under_sandbox (sleep 10 under 1s budget → timed-out result ~1s).

